(3) WHEN IS THE Z/2 ACTION FREE?  t=1/2 is the unique fixed point of t -> 1-t.
    At t=1/2: ||v/2|| = 0 if v EVEN, 1/2 if v ODD.  So t=1/2 is a maximizer
    exactly when ALL speeds are odd (then M = 1/2, the global maximum).

    family                     all odd?  M          1/2 a maximizer?  free?
    {1,...,13}                 False    1/14       False            True
    {1,3,5,...,25} all odd     True     1/2        True             False
    {1,3,...,23,26}            False    13/49      False            True
    {1..11,13,24}              False    1/14       False            True
    {1..11,13,36}              False    3/41       False            True

  => the free-Z/2 hypothesis of Borsuk-Ulam holds EXACTLY when the family
     contains an even speed.  All-odd families have the reflection-FIXED
     witness t = 1/2 with M = 1/2 -- Brouwer's regime, not Borsuk-Ulam's.
     (And all-odd families are trivial for LRC: 1/2 >> 1/14.)
